# StyleX inspector UI

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	import * as stylex from '@stylexjs/stylex';
	import { chrome } from '$lib/ui/shared/shell/chrome.style';
</script>

<h1 {...stylex.attrs(chrome.title)}>Requests</h1>
```

```svelte
<!-- BAD: React API, scoped CSS, new palette -->
<div className={stylex.props(styles.root).className}></div>
<style> h1 { color: tomato; } </style>
```

- Reset CSS (`$lib/ui/shared/reset.css`) must not set `color` on `a`. Unlayered CSS beats StyleX layers, so link color would never show.
- Create styles in colocated `*.style.ts` files or `$lib/ui/shared/`, not in `<style>`.
- Spread `stylex.attrs(...)`. Conditional: `stylex.attrs(base, on && extra)`.
